cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use λWAVES in a talk, a lesson or a paper, please cite it as below."
title: "λWAVES — a real-time WebGPU instrument for the hydrogen eigenstates and small molecules"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hosain
    given-names: Joshua
    affiliation: Magic Commons
version: 0.9.0-alpha
date-released: 2026-10-16
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: https://github.com/magic-commons/lambdawaves
url: https://lambdawaves.magic-commons.com
abstract: >-
  λWAVES reconstructs the 91 hydrogen eigenstates with n ≤ 6 from their closed forms on the GPU as a
  playable wave field, evolved field-free by their phases alone, and solves small molecules live
  (Hartree–Fock and Kohn–Sham LDA in vendored Gaussian bases) or opens them from a library of
  precomputed records, with a modulation rack, projects and shareable state links. Every system
  carries a status word: EXACT (a closed form), NUMERICAL (a solve checked against an oracle; for a
  molecule's energy, PySCF on the same atoms and basis) or UNCHECKED (no oracle). The GPU grid is
  held to the CPU in its own metric: hydrogen's |Δψ| RMS ≤ 3e-6 and worst voxel ≤ 2e-4; a molecule's
  density within 0.2 % of its maximum. Built with AI coding agents under the author's direction;
  see the README's disclosure.
keywords:
  - hydrogen
  - quantum mechanics
  - quantum chemistry
  - WebGPU
  - visualisation
  - scientific instrument
